---
import NewsArticleLayout from "../../layouts/NewsArticleLayout.astro";
import type { TocItem } from "../../components/ArticleToc.astro";

const toc: TocItem[] = [
  { id: "long-cycle-life", text: "Long cycle life", depth: 2 },
  { id: "inherent-stability", text: "Inherent stability", depth: 2 },
  { id: "cobalt-free", text: "Cobalt-free", depth: 2 },
];
---
<NewsArticleLayout
  title="Why we use LiFePO4 for home batteries"
  description="Why SunHestia chooses lithium iron phosphate (LiFePO4) cells for home battery storage: long life, stability and a cobalt-free supply chain."
  path="news/lifepo4-home-batteries"
  toc={toc}
>
  <div class="prose">
      <div style="color:var(--c-ink-soft); font-size:.9rem">2026-07 · SunHestia</div>
      <h1>Why we use LiFePO4 for home batteries</h1>
      <p>
        For a stationary home battery, the priorities are different from those of
        a phone or a car. Space and weight are rarely the constraint; lifespan,
        safety and cost per cycle are. That is why SunHestia uses lithium iron
        phosphate (LiFePO4) chemistry.
      </p>
      <h2 id="long-cycle-life">Long cycle life</h2>
      <p>
        LiFePO4 cells tolerate thousands of charge-discharge cycles with modest
        degradation. For a home battery that cycles daily, that translates into a
        long service life — which is why we can offer a 10-year warranty.
      </p>
      <h2 id="inherent-stability">Inherent stability</h2>
      <p>
        The chemistry is thermally stable and resistant to the conditions that
        drive degradation and failure in other lithium chemistries. That makes it
        well suited to a device that lives on a wall in a home for a decade.
      </p>
      <h2 id="cobalt-free">Cobalt-free</h2>
      <p>
        LiFePO4 contains no cobalt, which simplifies the supply chain and avoids a
        material associated with well-documented environmental and social
        concerns.
      </p>
      <p>
        The trade-off is a slightly lower energy density than some alternatives —
        but for a home battery that simply means a slightly larger enclosure, a
        reasonable price for the safety and longevity gained.
      </p>
    </div>
</NewsArticleLayout>
